main='''<main id="main"><div class="atlas-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Overview</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/evidence/">Evidence</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Support and phase data audit</span></div><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">21 October 2026 Chicago · Published-data audit 0.1</div><h1>Useful simulator data.<br>No action anchor admitted.</h1><p class="lede">Four experimental releases are reviewed against the energy-clock-support contract. A signed trace is useful evidence, but it does not itself supply the native support and energy map.</p></div>
<aside class="callout"><strong>Scoped content audit · Action-anchor HOLD · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>No hbar or η<sub>A</sub> estimate, bridge score or experiment is reported. Reviews have different file coverage. “Not established” refers to the inspected material, not proof that additional author records do not exist. Independent review is pending.</p></aside>
<div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/support-data-audit-v0.1/REPORT.md">Read scoped audit ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/support-data-audit-v0.1/DATASET_GATES.json">Inspect per-dataset gates</a></div>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Four releases, four bounded dispositions.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Release</th><th>Inspected material</th><th>Useful next role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://doi.org/10.11588/DATA/6MEKHI">Riechert circuit LGT</a></td><td>One raw waveform; acquisition documentation; static figures notebook</td><td>Signed reconstruction and parity diagnostics</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18012627">Datla Rydberg data</a></td><td>All 27 CSV members; paper and publication data statement</td><td>Correlator/localization reanalysis</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/3RXD5F">Yang optical-lattice data</a></td><td>Original Fig.4 workbook, four tabs</td><td>Population and gauge-violation comparisons</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8gtht76k2">Mil atomic-mixture data</a></td><td>One additional CSV text response; separate prior three-CSV audit</td><td>Population/imbalance response</td></tr></tbody></table><p>None of these scoped reviews establishes the complete same-carrier map, absolute native support, signed state clock, calibrated energy and joint uncertainty conjunction.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Squaring a circuit trace changes the spectral information.</h2><p>The hash-verified circuit waveform contains ten channels with 100 records each. The descriptive diagnostic uses only record zero of the nine live channels: subtract 200 initial samples, demean, apply a Hann window, and compare fixed high-frequency bands for V and V².</p><p>All nine squared-signal peak bins fall within one bin of twice the voltage peak. This illustrates the parity warning. It does not certify primitive recurrence, the native Hodge clock, or QPB1’s unrelated η<sub>A</sub>=2/1 prediction.</p><p>The notebook’s envelope-energy routine uses a nominal 20 nF capacitor. No independent absolute UD support map, full energy/baseline certificate or timing-skew uncertainty is established here. No imported code is executed.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/support-data-audit-v0.1/CIRCUIT_CONTENT_AUDIT.json">Read the bounded circuit diagnostic →</a></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>The newer Rydberg archive needs explicit axis handling.</h2><p>All 27 scientific CSV members parse as finite arrays. The bottom figure-2a time vector contains two identical copies of the 21-entry top vector, while the associated arrays are 31×21. The original data are preserved; any axis collapse needs a documented rule before fitting.</p><p>Mean-Z signs are signed expectations, not a field-phase witness. The inspected release does not establish an independent UD support or energy map. The 2026 publication links the public archive, improving on the older preprint’s on-request data statement.</p><p>Source CSV redistribution: Datla, Zhao, Ho, Klco and Loh; <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18012627">Zenodo source</a>, CC-BY-4.0. The derived bundle retains scientific CSV bytes and omits unrelated archive metadata.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/support-data-audit-v0.1/RYDBERG_CSV_SOURCE_v1.zip">Download attributed scientific CSV bundle ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/support-data-audit-v0.1/RYDBERG_CONTENT_AUDIT.json">Open archive content audit →</a></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Representation and calibration remain part of the evidence.</h2><p>Harvard’s original-format Fig.4 download is a four-tab Excel workbook despite the requested .tab filename. The original and ingested representations need their own byte counts and parsers. The Mil figure-4A response contains 22 numerical rows of normalized imbalance/population data; a direct-download access failure limits raw-byte verification.</p><p>Next, freeze signed-voltage reconstruction and keep fast carrier, rotating-frame envelope and quadratic energy distinct. Missing absolute amplitude, energy and phase-skew certificates stay OPEN. This tests reconstruction machinery without admitting a native-action anchor.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/energy-clock/">Read the governing energy-clock-support theorem →</a></div></section></main>'''
template=(dist/'evidence/energy-clock/index.html').read_text();page=re.sub(r'<title>.*?</title>','<title>Support and phase data audit · Unified Dynamics</title>',template,count=1);page=re.sub(r'<main\b[\s\S]*?</main>',lambda _:main,page,count=1);folder=dist/'evidence/support-data-audit';folder.mkdir(exist_ok=False);(folder/'index.html').write_text(page)
